Z||000000||Formula88||06-03-2001||01:29 AM||||Hey guys, I don't want to rain on your parade, but the animated sigs are getting a bit much.  Everytime I view a thread with these, my browser performance (and PC response in general) takes a serious nosedive.  I'm running a PII 800Mhz, with 256Mb CAS2 RAM, so hardware shouldn't be a problem.  It enough to make me not want to read a post from someone with an animated sig just because of the annoyance.  I guess, what I'm getting at, is, can we please ease up on these?  Maybe use it for your initial post but not every time you respond to a thread?  I really do like them, but it really does make reading the posts a PITA.  <P>Just my $.02.  Not meant to flame anyone.||||reg||13
Z||000001||FieroSTETZ||06-03-2001||03:48 AM||||people mostly need to remeber that not everyone has a cable modem - my sig started out pretty huge but now takes but a sec on 56k at my girlfriends house - use gifcon or something to reverse engineer the anigif and compress the files, make black and white, something. if my sig is still to big, i can get the mutha down to about 70k, but its a bit small then<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.shawnrocks.com/test.GIF"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroSTETZ||06-03-2001||03:49 AM||||besides, if that system is doing that, you have something wrong - my pocketpc shows the anigif just fine... some of them, the butt kicking one, really DOES drag down a system, needs every other frame chopped out||||reg||1
Z||000003||Nashco||06-03-2001||04:07 AM||||Formula88, I think you may have some problems with your operating system.  Perhaps you have some other programs running, or you need to reload windows due to some mixed up files, but something isn't right.<P>I'm running a PIII 600 mhz laptop with 128mb ram and an 8mb graphics card.  My computer doesn't even flinch.  Oh, I use windows 2k, which also uses more ram than earlier versions, so I'm working with much less ram than you.  I know for damn sure it isn't modem speed...because my service SUCKS down here in 'bama.<P>I don't mind the .gif files, but they do take a while to load.  FieroSTETZ, I'm sure you're proud of your file and you spent a lot of time on it, but it seems a little much.  It is very very quick...I'm worried I'll go into a seizure if I look directly at it.  You may want to think of something you find equally cool, but not so hard to look at.  AusFiero's isn't bad because it doesn't attract too much attention and can be ignored if you want to.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||7
Z||000004||AusFiero||06-03-2001||04:17 AM||||Thanks Nashco, but even I am going to tone it down a little to just the moving road and car. The text banner takes up most of the file size. It is about 54K now but I can take it down to 12K without the scrolling text. At 12K it will be a smaller sig file than most JPG ones.<P>Note signature left out of this thread for Formula88.<P>I am running the same system as you Formula88. I think you may have some problems as people have suggested. What video card are you running, video memory and is your web provider a modem connection or cable? <BR>I am using a modem conection and have no problems even with multiple programs, windows and browsers open.||||reg||1
