Z||000021||theogre||06-03-2001||04:10 PM||||There are allot of users who don't have highspeed access. It simply isn't available outside densly populated areas. Even in dense areas the services are not avalable in many places. Why? because the cable system is too old and so is the phone system. It will be years before many areas are upgraded. Even so called "56K" modems won't work in these areas above the older 33.6 standards. Putting high bandwidth items in forum threads just because you can doesn't mean you should.<P>Anigif sigs are mostly annoying and waste bandwidth. FieroStetz anigif is poor quality and huge. The WebTV folks must really find it a joy...<P>But since you brought it up 88formula, Sig Pics that are extremely tall are just as bad. Your's is one such example. At least you usually only use the thing once in a thread. Some people use the huge pictures over and over...<P>To make pics even worse... Animated or not... they are being pulled from all over the web. I'm sick of having forum pages chew forever becuse of some slow turd third party server that's hosting pics on it. This applies to all images, not just sigs but when you end up with sigs pulling from 6 diferant servers in the same thread, it really hoses page loads. I've had trouble loading such forum pages even on T1 and larger pipes. These problems aren't Cliff's fault. They are 100% forum member caused.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 06-03-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000022||Coconut||06-03-2001||05:15 PM||||I remember when Cliff first gave us the go ahead with the signature option...seemed like a great idea and a way to 'personalize' our posts. It now appears that it has been a bit too cumbersome and annoying and that is a shame when it prevents some of our members to access certain pages because of agonizingly long loading times. Don't get me wrong, I appreciate and enjoy some of the creative sigs I have seen, but is there a way we could make some of our sigs a bit simpler and still get your point across? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">I'd hate for Cliff to say that it indeed has gone way overboard...that was in fact one of his initial fears  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>Sometimes, less is more ...if you catch my drift! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Cruisin' <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Coconut's_Signature_1.JPG"> ||||reg||9
Z||000023||Formula88||06-03-2001||05:58 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by LZeitgeist:<BR><B>BABAHAHAHAH!! Sorry, guys... nothing personal, just thought this was slightly funny.<P>Formula88's a former NASA employee who's been making his daily living as a computer programmer/technician/troubleshooter for the last 15 years... :::chuckle::: I don't think there's anything wrong with his system...    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>(Of course, you guys had no way of knowing that, so I'm not laughing *at* you, I promise.)    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Guess I should have been wearing my "As a matter of fact, I AM a rocket scientist" t-shirt.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><P>And, BTW, all of the sigs on this post so far don't cause any slow down.  Has anyone else had this problem?  Or is it just me?  <p>[This message has been edited by Formula88 (edited 06-03-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000024||Black88GT||06-03-2001||06:03 PM||||I remember Cliff made a post about this in the Announcement section.  I have referenced this to many people in the past but they just ignore it.  <P>It's reminding me of the Corvette Forum.  Everyone has huge pics of their cars in their sigs and scrolling down the page is a pain.  The smaller sigs arent bad but some people cross the line with huge pics and now animated gifs...||||reg||1
Z||000025||Formula88||06-03-2001||06:05 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by theogre:<BR><B>But since you brought it up 88formula, Sig Pics that are extremely tall are just as bad. Your's is one such example. At least you usually only use the thing once in a thread. Some people use the huge pictures over and over...<BR>(edited 06-03-2001).]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Ah, I agree completely.  You may have noticed I don't use a sig pic anymore, unless there's a specific reason to post a pic of my car.  When I get one small enough, that I still like, then I may start using one again.<P>Good point on the multiple sigs, etc., too.  With PIP, that's the easiest way to post stuff on here, and it's gotta be faster than links to all over.<BR>||||reg||14
Z||000026||Urchin||06-03-2001||06:12 PM||||I don't have any problems with them, but I guess I can thank my cable modem for that  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>I think that there are two sides to this though.  1. Why should you not be able to express creative ideas because of other's bad connections.<BR>At the same time 2.  Why should those with bad connections have to suffer because they don't  have the same privilages some of the others do.<BR>I can see both sides and don't like the idea of this being a problem <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature2_3.jpg">   <P>If you can read this, I'm parked.||||reg||1
Z||000027||FieroSTETZ||06-04-2001||03:57 AM||||what about this one?<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.shawnrocks.com/Animation1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000028||theogre||06-04-2001||01:23 PM||||That little one is much better Stetz. 47-48K is a heck of allot faster loading than 285K. It looks better smaller as well. Not as fuzzy.<P>88, Like I said, Most of the time you usually only used it once. Imagine that size image 10 times in a 20 message thread. It doesn't happen often hear yet but it's a really huge pain on other systems. My hope is to prevent such a thing happening here. <P>I don't mind small sigs but at the same time does anyone really want to see the same sig multiple times in a thread? Even nice sigs get old if they are over used. It's like songs on a top 40 radio station... Even the really good ones start to s--k after you hear them 300 time in a week.<P>Other's, Good point 88. For those of you that can, Using PIP to post images to Cliff's servers would help considerably. (If you can't PIP them there are a number of people who would probably help you. Just ask.) Then everything comes from the same place a much as posible an we won't get pounded by slow/dead third party servers. Also, images posted to cliffs server will be included in Cliff's Forum CD. Images from other sites may not make it on the disk. This can really kill the usability of allot of threads. (This would apply to all images not just sig pics...)<P>Me I forget about PIP since I don't post many images. Fortunatly the little I do post is usually Cave Article material so you can still view it by going there. (The cutaway rear brake piston is a perfect example of me forgeting about PIP again...)<P>I'm not out to kill people getting creative. Those people just need to keep in mind many people have no choice about how they access the forum. I'm betting that's the majority of users. Me, I have high speed at work, but the connection is monitored and the forum is a policy violation so I can't do much from there. At home I'm still forced to use a 33.6 modem because the phone company doesn't have DSL service in this area yet. Cable is out becuase I will not be forced to use Comcast as my ISP. (Mote point Since they told me my cable doesn't support it yet anyway...) <P>The big reason I don't want to move, It takes considerable time and effort to convert everything in my cave from one server to another. The multiple migrations of Spry servers as the system was sold to AOL then Mindspring then Earthlink has caused me days of work fixing problems in the cave. At one point I had to rework nearly every single page to fix something or another that broke.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 06-04-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000029||DRH||06-04-2001||01:25 PM||||Still reminds me of an banner ad. The movement bothers me more than the load time. If I'm trying to read something, catching all that motion out of the corner of my eye is annoying.<P>Cliff mentioned a little while back he was having to do hardware/network upgrades because of the traffic. I wonder how much of that traffic is caused by the proliferation of graphics (especially animated) in signatures? You can put a LOT of text in tha same amount of space as even a fairly small animated graphics file...||||reg||13
